
  <sn><md>### Understanding Rclone Remotes

A **remote** is one of the most important concepts in Rclone.

In simple terms:

&gt; A remote is a `name` that Rclone uses to **represent a configured storage location.**

For example, you can configure your Google Drive and give it the name `gdrive`:

```text
gdrive:
```

Then Rclone uses `gdrive:` to access that Google Drive.
</md></sn>
