<sn><md>### Remote Structure

The general format is:

```text
remote-name:path
```

For example:

```text
gdrive:Documents/Notes
```

| Part            | Example                  | Meaning                         |
| --------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------- |
| Remote name     | `gdrive`                 | Name of the configured remote   |
| `:`             | `:`                      | Separates remote name from path |
| Remote path     | `Documents/Notes`        | Location inside the remote      |
| Complete remote | `gdrive:Documents/Notes` | Full Rclone path                |
</md></sn><sn><md>### Remote Is Not the Cloud Account Itself

Suppose you have a Google Drive account.

You configure it in Rclone and give it the name:

```text
gdrive
```

The relationship is:

```text
Rclone
  │
  └── gdrive
        │
        ▼
   Google Drive
```

The name `gdrive` is simply **your local Rclone configuration name**.

You could instead call it:

```text
study
```

Then:

```text
study:
```

would refer to that same Google Drive.

You could even call it:

```text
my-cloud
```

Then:

```text
my-cloud:
```

would work.

</md></sn>